<!--
  CLI Documentation — TransformCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.TransformCommand
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:cli="org.blockml.bml.cli"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:cliconfig="org.blockml.bml.cli.config"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:runtime="org.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime"
  xmlns:framework="org.blockml.bml.framework"
  xmlns:transformer="org.blockml.bml.transformer"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>TransformCommand</name>
  <type>clidocumentation:TransformCommand</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>blockml transform specification</is>

  <documentation><![CDATA[Syntax:
    blockml transform apply EXECUTION-FQN [--library path] [--verbose] [--parameters JSON] [--parameter-mappings JSON]

    transform is a parent command. V1 defines the apply subcommand only.
    Further transform subcommands are declared on clicommand:TransformCommand
    subcommands.

    EXECUTION-FQN is a ModelTransformation Apply source:
    {library}._meta.transform.pending (template=false, source moved),
    {library}._meta.transform.available (template=true, source stays),
    or any FQN outside _meta.transform (template=true, source stays).
    Other _meta.transform packages are rejected. Tasks are not accepted
    directly.

    Target library for `_meta` is --library (a path to that library's
    Library.bml). Omitted: package.json blockml.library of the current
    working directory. Missing both is exit 2. Distinct from --libraries
    (registry seeds). In a multi-package repo, cwd selects the default
    target library.

    --parameters is JSON of any value. StructType: merged over pending
    (CLI wins; nested objects merge; arrays replace). Other types: CLI
    replaces pending. Prepare checks the result against bound T (default
    type:Text) and writes a value only when one exists (not "" / {}).
    Omitted --parameters is no overlay. --parameter-mappings is a JSON
    array of ParameterMapping objects; a non-empty CLI array wins over
    pending parameterMappings and ignores --parameters.

    The transformer takes an exclusive worktree lock, then prepares the
    ModelTransformation and runs each ModelOperation in order: persist
    operation Running, dispatch the registered OperationExecutor,
    Reflect, Persist results onto that operation. Default
    Prepare/Finalize are deterministic. Default executor for
    AgenticOperation is AgenticExecutor (Claude Code) that changes BML
    only. Default executor for ToolOperation is ToolExecutor (npm CLI
    via npx). Default Reflect is deterministic (git changedFiles after the)
    executor; output when ModelOperation.captureOutput is true). Default
    Persist writes those fields onto the operation.
    Finalize relocates to _meta.transform.succeeded only when every
    ModelOperation succeeded and result resolution did not throw;
    otherwise _meta.transform.failed and a
    non-zero exit. A failed ModelOperation aborts the rest.

    Lifecycle lines (ModelTransformation and operation status,
    execute/reflect start and done) always print so progress is visible
    without --verbose.

    Only one transform may run at a time in the same Git worktree. A second
    call fails immediately (exit 2) with no wait. Different worktrees may
    run in parallel.

    --verbose streams additional agent-session detail (thinking, tools, text).
    It does not control the lifecycle lines.

    The worktree must be clean at start and before each ModelOperation
    (exit 2 otherwise). Prepare records baseCommit from HEAD and commits
    the running relocation. Each ModelOperation commits Running first,
    then commits model changes with the operation terminal state. Finalize commits the
    succeeded or failed relocation.

    Pending-contract violations never start the execution (exit 2).

Printed help:
Usage: blockml transform apply <execution-fqn> [--library path] [--verbose] [--parameters json] [--parameter-mappings json]
       blockml transform --help

When: run a ModelTransformation.

transform is a parent command. V1 defines apply only.
EXECUTION-FQN is a pending one-shot, an available template, or a template outside _meta.transform.
--library is a path to the target Library.bml. Omitted: cwd package.json blockml.library. Missing both is exit 2.

Pipeline stage constraints belong to the Execute / Reflect prompts, not here.

Flags:
  --library path    target Library.bml for _meta (default: cwd package.json blockml.library)
  --verbose         stream additional agent-session detail
  --parameters json           JSON value for parameters (object merge when T is StructType)
  --parameter-mappings json   JSON array of ParameterMapping objects; ignores --parameters

Only one transform may run at a time in the same Git worktree.
The worktree must be clean at start and before each ModelOperation.

Related: validate, inspect.]]></documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:Commands" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicommand:TransformCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicommand:TransformApplyCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:RunTransform" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>

</block>
